Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:36:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 363/365] DOS-PORT: patch 0363 -- lever 1: skip the per-tick
 update of a character that provably cannot change

Every tick UpdateCharacterMoveAndAnim and its five callees run for every 'on' character in the game
-- 102 on MMD, 101 of them in other rooms (~1.24 ms/tick on the 486, F1a). For a character in
another room that is not turning, not moving, not following anyone, and whose (view, loop, frame)
were validated by the last full update and are unchanged, that update does exactly one thing:
process_idle_this_time = 0. The skip does that and nothing else; any other character, and the
first tick after any of those fields changes, takes the full update (which re-records the triple).

Behind DOSAGS_ENGLEV=1 here (0365 makes it the default; 0 is the fallback); read once with the
VM mode. Lab-only (-DDOSAGS_VMTRACE, DOSAGS_ENGLEV_SHADOW=1): for every skipped character the full
update still runs on a copy and the whole CharacterInfo/CharacterExtras state, the follower list
and the number of Random() draws are compared ("charskip MISMATCH"); statewit gains el= and rnd=.

Lab (docs/lab/LEVERS-REPORT.md sections 5-12): 0 mismatches over 751,085 skipped updates on MMD
character select, the MMD intro, AGS Quest (with restore) and seeded 5 Days; RNG draws unchanged;
digests EQUAL to legacy on all four; game_objects_update 0.569 -> 0.145 ms/tick at fixed 40k.

